ll macro spatial extents>=3, auxiliary charge1, actual C=positiveT4 operator identity already captured. No noncentral colour or interacting Phi bound.\",\n    \"exact_charge_graph_identity\": \"chi_jk(eta)=det(I+Deta^-1 Rj\\u2020Deta Rk)/sqrt(det(I+Rj\\u2020Rj)det(I+Rk\\u2020Rk)). It includes centered e^-2i sumeta algebraically, not omitted background.\",\n    \"occupied_graph_bound\": \"Bmin=b-3,b=1/(2k), ||F||<=3. Top-subspace Sylvester gives ||X||<=||E||/gap with gap=Bmin-1/Bmin, ||E||<=3/Bmin. If this ratio<=1/2, ||R||<=2||E||/gap. No arbitrary fullrank/Gram assumption.\",\n    \"expansion\": \"R0=-b^-2 F. Riccati gives ||R-R0||<=9/(b Bmin)*(1/Bmin+1/b)+(10*rbound+3*rbound\\u00b2)/Bmin\\u00b2.\",\n    \"characteristic_bound\": \"Uniform all eta and arbitrary mixed Abelian spatial phases: |NF logchi_jk-beta sumedges[cos(eta_x-eta_y+delta_theta_xy)-1]| <=2V NF[4*r0*eps+2eps\\u00b2+rbound^4/(1-rbound\\u00b2)]. beta=16NF k4; genuine macro has no length2/selfedge degeneracy.\",\n    \"uniform_macro_log_character_error\": \"4.080124641199373464633344e-76\",\n    \"NF_Covrho_over_beta_leading\": \"graphL, derived from R0 spin blocks: each oriented neighbor ||R0xy||F\\u00b2=8k4, paired edges16k4. No nearestDirac assumption.\",\n    \"covariance_quadratic_remainder_per_site_for_unit_sup_charge_direction\": \"1.728e-247\",\n    \"positive_HS_relative_Gram_bound\": \"Leading chi_jk=exp(beta sum cosminus1) is nonnegative. With positive normalized HS Gaussian, multiplicative character remainder gives relative Gram error<=exp(delta)-1 despite tiny preparation norm. This does NOT normalize an arbitrary signed/global projected source.\",\n    \"exact_leading_charge_kernel\": \"Glead_jk=E_eta exp[beta sumedges(cos(eta_x-eta_y+delta_theta_xy)-1)], eta covariance2u Lplus, u=.02. Entire periodic HS integral retained; Gaussian saddle alone is not the exact finite-beta expression.\",\n    \"coexact_small_phase_prediction\": \"For canonical deltaA=sqrtbeta*deltatheta with incidence*deltaA=0, local Gaussian saddle gives normalized Gjk\\u2248exp(-||deltaA||\\u00b2/2). Gradient metric is1/[2(1+2u beta)]. This is a conditional asymptotic prediction; aliases, volumeuniform saddle and actual compressed core consumer need separate control.\",\n    \"prep_cost_prediction\": \"Gaussian charge approximation gives Gram\\u2248(1+2u beta)^(-(V-1)/2); discrete charge/periodic HS aliases require their theta-function factor, so this expression is NOT asserted as exact macro preparation cost.\",\n    \"uncompressed_warning\": \"Coulomb chargefilter produces a non-Slater output; its norm and complement cannot be inferred from bare sea overlap.\",\n    \"scope\": \"Actual finiteNF Coul/HS character and preparation controls plus uniform Riccati charge-character bound. Not complete realGauss/source/current or physicalmass1 admission.\"\n  }\n}\n",
